        <body>
            <div xml:id="d914">

                <pb facs="0716" n="600" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg600"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13217.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-18T17:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 18, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s September 17, 6 p.m. In conference with General Carranza this
                    afternoon, he confirms the information furnished Department by me through
                    Brazilian Minister last night: General Candido Aguilar has been appointed to
                    receive the entire federal and municipal government of Vera Cruz from the
                    American authorities. He is fully empowered to name the persons who are to
                    assume charge of all posts both federal and municipal. General Carranza awaits
                    the Department’s information as to when it will be appropriate for General
                    Aguilar to proceed to Vera Cruz with his staff. He also requests that if it
                    meets the Department’s approval I be permitted to accompany General Aguilar to
                    Vera Cruz in order to duly present him to General Funston.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
